  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nYou have two scripts that modify `document.body.className`:\n  ```html\n  <body onload=\"document.body.className = 'failed'\">\n  <script>document.body.className = 'loading'</script>\n  ```\n  - The inline script sets the class to `loading` immediately as the HTML is parsed.\n  - The `onload` handler then sets it to `failed` **after the whole page loads**.\n\n  **Issue:**  \n  Modern browsers parse and execute `<script>` tags as they are encountered. However, when the `<script>` is placed before `<body>`, `document.body` may be `null` at that point, causing `document.body.className` to fail silently or do nothing.\n",
